# Deploy @@APP_NAME@@ in the AI Trust Platform — UI guide

GENERATED by `marketplace/tools/prepare-app`. Copy-paste checklist to add **@@APP_NAME@@** to the
Marketplace through the UI. Every field value is filled in for this app.

---

## Prerequisites

Before you start, make sure you have:

1. **Platform Administrator access** — you need the `marketplace:manage` permission to see the Marketplace
   nav item. Sign in and verify the **Marketplace** item appears in the sidebar.

2. **A published image** — the repo's **Actions** tab must show a green `publish-image` run after a push
   to the `@@BRANCH@@` branch, and the package `ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:@@IMAGE_TAG@@` must exist under
   **Packages**. *(If CI is still failing, see `marketplace/Implementation/03-publish-image.md`.)*

3. **A GitHub `read:packages` PAT** *(if the GHCR package is private)* — create one at
   **GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens** with scope `read:packages`.
   It is used only to pull the image; it is never stored by the platform.

4. **Multi-tenant deployment?** — if your platform is a mesh/MSP tenant (you log in against a per-tenant
   Keycloak realm such as `test`, not the built-in `ai-trust` realm), read
   `marketplace/Implementation/05-multitenant-mesh-notes.md` **before** deploying — one backend env var
   must match your tenant's realm or SSO will fail.

---

## Step 1 — Add the service

Marketplace → **"Add a service (internal — deployed on this cluster)"**:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Display name** | `@@APP_NAME@@` |
| **Slug (URL-safe)** | `@@SLUG@@` |
| **Type** (radio cards) | **Server app — prebuilt image** |
| **Image reference** | `ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:@@IMAGE_TAG@@` |
| **App port** | `@@REGISTER_PORT@@` |
| **Platform SSO** | @@PLATFORM_SSO_FIELD@@ |
| **Open in a new tab** | ⬜ leave unticked (embedded) |
| **Private registry** | ✅ tick *(untick only if the package is public)* |
| **Environment variables (optional)** | leave empty — the platform injects OIDC settings |

Click **Add to catalog**. A card appears with status `pending`.

> **Why this port?**
> - **Sidecar mode (Path A):** port `@@REGISTER_PORT@@` is the sidecar's listen port. The app runs
>   internally on `@@UPSTREAM_PORT@@` and is never exposed directly.
> - **JWT-trust mode (Path B):** port `@@REGISTER_PORT@@` is the app's own port — there is no sidecar.

---

## Step 2 — Deploy

Click **Deploy**. With **Private registry** ticked, the form reveals **Registry username** (your GitHub
username) and **Registry token / password** (the `read:packages` PAT from Prerequisites step 3 — *used
only to pull the image, never stored*). Fill both, click **Deploy** again → status changes to `running`.

---

## Step 3 — Enable for a role

When `running`, click **Enable for role…** → pick a role (e.g. **Platform Administrator**) → **Apply**.
The tile is hidden from all users until at least one role is enabled.

---

## Step 4 — Use it

The tile appears under **Services** in the sidebar for users in the enabled role. Click it → it opens
embedded → you are logged in via the **platform**. No second login.

> **JWT-trust apps (Path B):** the app receives the user's identity as a `Bearer` JWT in the
> `Authorization` header. The patched `requireAuth` (`.platform-sso/rbac-platform-patch.js`) reads it
> and establishes a session — the app's own login page is never shown.

---

## Verify the configuration (optional)

Click **Configuration** on the card:

```
Kind          image
Image ref     ghcr.io/@@REPO@@:@@IMAGE_TAG@@
App port      @@REGISTER_PORT@@
Open mode     same window (embedded)
Platform SSO  @@PLATFORM_SSO_FIELD@@
```

